Subject: Cantor Tool Discovery and Addressed Deliberation

Description: Cantor as an inference-tool framework that stages semantic capability loading, assigns verified participant addresses, and coordinates point, counterpoint, and reconciliation through typed multi-pass deliberation rather than uninspectable simulated voices.

& [NormalToolCallingComparison] is the boundary with ordinary LLM tools
  + [tool_definition] is a name, description, input schema, and application-owned implementation made available to a model
  + [tool_call] is a model-produced request naming a tool and arguments
  + [tool_execution] is the host application validating and executing the request
  + [tool_output] is a call-correlated result returned to a later model continuation
  + [ordinary_strength] is access to external data and actions through narrow typed operations
  + [ordinary_limit] is the tool contract usually does not itself define semantic purpose, attention behavior, faculty judgment, deliberation identity, or proof-carrying reconciliation
  = conclusion: Cantor contains ordinary tool calling but extends it with compiled semantic programs, staged frames, participant identity, addressed deliberation, validation, and provenance
  - never: treat a model-emitted tool call as proof that the call is valid, authorized, or semantically appropriate

& [CantorToolFramework] is the semantic meta-tool plane
  + [capability_registry] is admitted operations, FacultyPrograms, contracts, participant roles, provider requirements, schemas, and package digests
  + [discovery] is purpose and subject resolution to the minimum relevant capability descriptors
  + [loading] is admission of exact operation schemas and governing SOP into the active frame
  + [invocation] is a typed request bound to participant, purpose, frame, authority, and budget
  + [execution] is deterministic operation, provider inference, faculty activation, or composed workflow
  + [validation] is schema, trust, evidence, authority, Honesty, Security, and anti-enchantment checking
  + [coordination] is routing validated outputs among addressed participants and Observer
  + [proof] is complete source, call, message, derivation, decision, and effect lineage
  = must: separate discovering a capability from gaining authority to invoke or act through it
  = must: expose the smallest sufficient capability surface for the active purpose

& [CantorCallTriggerPolicy] is when a reasoning participant must call Cantor
  + [unbound_meaning] is a material term, relationship, proposition, or contextual anchor is missing or ambiguous
  + [governing_contract] is a condition, prohibition, required operation, or continuation may apply
  + [faculty_pressure] is truth, security, memory, refinement, planning, weaving, or reconciliation judgment is materially required
  + [artifact_need] is a source, specification, proof, history, or implementation artifact is missing
  + [conflict] is evidence, perspectives, instructions, associations, or authority disagree
  + [consequence] is a conclusion or action crosses a declared consequence threshold
  + [frame_change] is new material may require append, reframe, or capsule reset
  + [direct_request] is the principal or governing SOP requires Cantor participation
  = must: encode these triggers in the slim primer and FacultyPrograms
  - never: rely only on the model remembering to call Cantor after it has already adopted an unsupported conclusion

& [ToolLoadingPipeline] is staged Cantor capability admission
  + [stage_1_bootstrap] is load only the Cantor namespace identity, slim primer, discovery operation, and mandatory call triggers
  + [stage_2_preflight] is scan purpose, subject, consequence, actions, ambiguity, and likely faculty pressure
  + [stage_3_discover] is resolve candidate operations, participants, schemas, and required SOP dependencies
  + [stage_4_admit] is verify signatures, digests, versions, authority scope, provider compatibility, and budget
  + [stage_5_load] is project the minimum exact operation descriptions and attention programs into context
  + [stage_6_ready] is apply the FrameReadinessGate with the loaded capability manifest
  + [stage_7_invoke] is accept model or manager calls only from the admitted set
  + [stage_8_expand] is demand-load another capability when a new valid trigger appears
  = must: preserve cache-friendly stable bootstrap content where the provider supports it
  = must: make every dynamic load a visible frame transition
  - never: load the full Cantor capability library into every inference context

& [ProviderToolDiscoveryAdapter] is the provider-specific loading boundary
  + [native_tool_search] is use provider-supported deferred tool discovery when available
  + [generic_Cantor_discovery] is use one stable cantor discovery operation that returns signed capability descriptors when native search is absent
  + [static_projection] is preselect a bounded tool set before the model call for providers that require complete schemas up front
  + [programmatic_batch] is use code-mediated tool composition only for bounded predictable processing that does not require fresh semantic judgment between results
  = must: normalize all discovery modes to one Cantor capability manifest
  = must: use direct checkpointed inference when each result may change the next judgment
  - never: let provider convenience change the authoritative meaning of a Cantor operation

& [ParticipantAddress] is the verified identity of one deliberation participant
  + [runtime_uuid] is the supervising runtime epoch
  + [participant_uuid] is immutable participant identity within that runtime
  + [display_alias] is a human-readable session-unique name such as Honesty, Security, Planner-A, Codex-Builder-2, or Observer
  + [role] is the signed FacultyProgram, manager, worker, reviewer, or other admitted purpose
  + [principal_and_commission] is the authority lineage when agency exists
  + [package_and_program_digest] is the exact semantic and behavioral identity
  + [session_and_frame_digest] is the active context identity
  + [operation_scope] is the participant's permitted calls and message kinds
  + [authentication] is the runtime binding, credential, signature, or local process identity needed to prevent impersonation
  = must: route by immutable address rather than display alias alone
  = must: require display aliases to be unique within the visible deliberation
  = may: allow a participant to propose an alias
  - never: allow self-naming to create role, authority, package admission, or trusted identity

& [ParticipantRegistry] is the authoritative session directory
  + [registration] is manager or runtime admission of ParticipantAddress and capability manifest
  + [discovery_description] is a short purpose, subject, available judgment, and call condition
  + [status] is proposed, admitted, active, waiting, yielded, stopped, revoked, faulted, or expired
  + [mailbox] is ordered addressed messages and durable cursor
  + [visibility] is which participants may discover, address, or observe this participant
  + [revocation] is immediate invalidation of further calls and messages
  = must: resolve aliases to exact addresses before message projection
  = must: reject unknown, ambiguous, stale, spoofed, or out-of-scope recipients

| [DeliberationMoveKind] is (point | counterpoint | support | challenge | question | answer | distinction | association | counterassociation | qualification | concession | synthesis | objection | proposal | vote | yield | stop)

& [DeliberationMove] is one typed contribution to negotiated meaning
  + [move_uuid] is immutable move identity
  + [from] is exact ParticipantAddress
  + [to] is one participant, a bounded group, Observer, or the deliberation session
  + [kind] is DeliberationMoveKind
  + [subject] is the exact semantic anchor under discussion
  + [proposition] is the claim, distinction, association, or proposed transition
  + [target_move] is the point or counterpoint being answered when applicable
  + [attention_directives] is how the recipient should focus, bind, compare, challenge, or preserve the subject
  + [support] is evidence, source, derivation, authority, or test anchors
  + [uncertainty] is confidence limits, missing evidence, and unresolved alternatives
  + [requested_response] is expected move kind, output schema, budget, and stopping condition
  + [frame_digest] is the semantic frame under which the move was formed
  = must: distinguish evidence from persuasion and association from entailment
  = must: pass through Cantor validation before becoming active deliberation state
  - never: accept a counterpoint merely because it is rhetorically opposed

& [ExternalDeliberationLedger] is the authoritative shared cognition state
  + [participant_registry] is the admitted identity and capability set
  + [move_graph] is addressed point, counterpoint, support, challenge, response, and synthesis relations
  + [frame_history] is every attention projection and material change
  + [turn_state] is speaker eligibility, pending responses, barriers, budgets, and token ownership when used
  + [decision_state] is accepted, rejected, qualified, unresolved, superseded, or escalated propositions
  + [proof_state] is sources, validations, faculty reviews, and causal contribution
  = must: exist outside model hidden state
  = must: remain the authority for what was actually said, answered, and decided
  - never: infer shared participant knowledge merely because text appeared in one model's context

& [AttentionStreamProjection] is the bounded model-visible deliberation view
  + [recipient_identity] is the receiving ParticipantAddress and role
  + [current_subject] is the focused semantic anchor
  + [purpose] is the local deliberation duty
  + [pertinent_moves] is addressed messages and necessary surrounding point-counterpoint context
  + [attention_program] is the receiving faculty or agent directives
  + [response_contract] is the required DeliberationMove shape
  + [residual] is unresolved differences and carried uncertainty
  = must: project only the materially pertinent ledger slice
  = must: label sender, recipient, move identity, support, and frame digest
  = must: treat the projection as transient context rather than the durable record

& [MultiPassDeliberationCycle] is negotiated association through inference checkpoints
  + [pass_1_project] is Cantor prepares a participant-specific attention stream
  + [pass_2_infer] is the participant forms one or more candidate DeliberationMoves
  + [pass_3_validate] is Cantor checks identity, schema, support, authority, truthfulness, scope, and frame
  + [pass_4_route] is accepted moves append to the ledger and addressed recipients receive mailbox updates
  + [pass_5_counter] is recipients receive new projections and form answers, counterpoints, or revised associations
  + [pass_6_observe] is Observer compares causal contributions, preserved differences, evidence, gates, and purpose
  + [pass_7_continue] is dispatch another pass, request evidence, reframe, reconcile, yield, or stop
  + [pass_8_freeze] is bind the final or unresolved state into an InferenceCapsule
  = must: allow independent passes to run concurrently when they do not depend on each other's outputs
  = must: serialize dependent point-counterpoint moves through validated checkpoints
  = conclusion: genuine multi-participant deliberation is logically multi-pass even when a provider hides several passes inside one higher-level request

& [SimulatedAndGenuineDeliberationBoundary] is the participation distinction
  + [simulated_panel] is one model generates multiple named voices inside one uninterrupted response
  + [structured_role_passes] is one model performs separately framed sequential participant activations
  + [isolated_participants] is separate contexts, jobs, models, or deterministic faculties exchange addressed moves
  + [genuine_requirement] is identity, independent opportunity to object, causal influence, validation, answer obligation, and durable trace
  = may: use a simulated panel for brainstorming
  = must: label it as one model's simulation rather than independent agreement
  = should: use isolated participants for consequential disagreement, adversarial review, or correlated-failure reduction

& [CandidateCantorToolNamespace] is the non-authoritative stable surface
  + [discover] is find purpose-relevant capabilities and participants
  + [open] is create a digest-bound session or participant activation
  + [query] is retrieve signed semantic records, operations, and proof
  + [message] is submit an addressed DeliberationMove
  + [receive] is read validated mailbox moves and current projection
  + [review] is run faculty and Observer validation over a candidate state
  + [close] is freeze result, residual, and proof and terminate the session
  = should: remain a small stable namespace while capabilities and participant roles are data-driven
  - never: encode every Cantor participant as a permanent global tool name

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable tool and deliberation collection
  + [CTD-001] is extend ordinary tool calling with signed semantic programs, attention framing, participant identity, addressed deliberation, validation, and proof
  + [CTD-002] is define mandatory Cantor call triggers before unsupported conclusions form
  + [CTD-003] is stage tool bootstrap, discovery, admission, loading, readiness, invocation, and expansion
  + [CTD-004] is adapt native tool search, generic discovery, static projection, and bounded programmatic batching to one capability manifest
  + [CTD-005] is assign every participant an immutable address and session-unique human alias
  + [CTD-006] is prohibit self-declared names from creating trusted identity or authority
  + [CTD-007] is represent point and counterpoint as typed addressed DeliberationMoves
  + [CTD-008] is keep the authoritative deliberation ledger outside hidden model state
  + [CTD-009] is conduct dependent deliberation through validated multiple passes
  + [CTD-010] is distinguish simulated voices, structured role passes, and genuine isolated participation

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the tool-discovery and deliberation justification record
  + [fold_1_subject] is Cantor as an all-purpose inference-tool framework supporting named multi-agent point and counterpoint
  + [fold_2_boundary] is typed semantic orchestration and projected attention inside; uninspectable hidden-state negotiation, self-authorized naming, and decorative consensus outside
  + [fold_3_data_design] is capability, trigger, load manifest, participant address, registry, mailbox, deliberation move, move graph, attention projection, pass, and proof
  + [fold_4_governance] is signed admission, minimum loading, immutable routing, anti-spoofing, evidence distinction, Observer review, and multi-pass checkpointing
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is bootstrap, preflight, discover, admit, load, ready, invoke, route, counter, observe, and freeze
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is tool flooding, missed trigger, identity collision, alias spoofing, self-authority, context-only memory, forced consensus, unvalidated counterpoint, and pass explosion
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is interface and deliberation architecture formed while implementation remains behind the core, CLI, and single-participant proofs

